      "slug": "overview",
      "title": "apex Overview",
      "description": "What apex is: a modernised acme (three-button mouse, tags, columns, B2 execute, B3 look, plumbing) with a client–server split, embedded terminals for coding agents, remote attach over ssh, and a tool API that does not need 9P. Covers the main features, the three kinds of process (the apexd daemon, the gpui UI client, and tools and the CLI), and a map of the workspace crates, the Go SDK, providers, the mac bundle and the design documents (DESIGN.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, WEB.md, MODERN.md). Later pages cover the details; this one gives the big picture and where each part lives.",
