    {
      "slug": "sessions-and-replication",
      "title": "Sessions, Shards and Leadership",
      "description": "The model the whole system rests on: sessions, attachments and connections; state split into shards (buffer, window, layout, term, metalog, registry), each a replicated log; leasable versus pinned shards; leaders that sequence entries and followers that replay them; leases, fence epochs, transfer and reclaim (single-player mode). Explains why views live in the buffer shard and how ids are allocated without coordination. The entry types and apply are on the next page; the wire protocol is on attach-protocol.",
