      "slug": "cli",
      "title": "The apex Command",
      "description": "apex-cli, the stable public surface for scripts: Go-style flags, APEX_SOCKET and APEX_SESSION, and the subcommands (server, ls, stop, attach, new, open, win, text, edit, sel, exec, events, term, ps, kill, plumb, B, env, set, cat, io, tool, label, awd). Explains that each subcommand attaches as a tool with its own replica and proposes to the leader, so it works with no UI, plus apex-editor and xdg-open links. Profiles and settings are on the configuration page.",
